The engine must inspect the sheet and identify the correct header row.

Do not assume headers always start in row 1.

The Trial Balance may contain:

Repeated headers
Pivot tables
Subtotals
Grand totals
Blank rows
Merged cells
Repeated account descriptions
Currency sections
Amounts in original IQD
Amounts divided by 1,000
Very small rounding residuals
Positive and negative balances

The process must distinguish valid account-level rows from:

Headers
Subtotal rows
Grand Total rows
Currency labels
Formatting rows
Blank template rows

The preferred Trial Balance schema is:

