8. RECONCILIATION CALCULATIONS
============================================================

For each BS Mapping category calculate:

TB Mapped Total
= Sum of Adjusted Balance for all mapped accounts

TB Presentation Value
= TB Mapped Total × TB Presentation Sign Multiplier

Submission Normalized Value
= Raw Submission Value
  × Unit Multiplier
  × Submission Sign Multiplier

Absolute Difference
= TB Presentation Value
  - Submission Normalized Value

Use the following percentage variance:

Percentage Variance
= Absolute Difference / ABS(TB Presentation Value)

If TB Presentation Value is zero:

1. If both TB and submission equal zero, variance is zero.
2. If TB equals zero and submission is non-zero, variance must be flagged as undefined or infinite.
3. Do not return a misleading zero percentage.

Support both:

Absolute tolerance
Percentage tolerance

Recommended status logic:

PASS:
Absolute difference is within absolute tolerance
OR percentage variance is within percentage tolerance

REVIEW:
Difference exceeds tolerance but both values were successfully extracted

MISSING_SUBMISSION:
No valid submission amount was extracted

UNMAPPED_TB:
Relevant TB accounts remain unmapped

DUPLICATE_MAPPING:
At least one account is mapped to multiple categories

UNIT_UNCONFIRMED:
Submission unit could not be established

SIGN_UNCONFIRMED:
Presentation-sign treatment is not configured

EXTRACTION_AMBIGUOUS:
More than one possible submission line was identified

ERROR:
A technical or structural failure prevents completion

Do not classify a category as PASS if any material extraction or mapping exception affects it.

